# Generated sentence timing for the checked-in narration.

[[scene]]
file = "scene-01.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Welcome to Xmip, an open-source messaging and integration platform written \
in Rust.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 5.625

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
It is on premises first and cloud installable, so organizations choose \
where their integration runs.\
"""
start = 5.805
duration = 6.575

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
This is the Xmip project story: what it connects, how it records \
responsibility, and how people design and operate it.\
"""
start = 12.56
duration = 7.825

[[scene]]
file = "scene-02.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip is being developed for organizations that need dependable messaging \
and integration under their own control.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 8.35

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
It carries forward familiar integration concepts while putting deployment \
and data under organizational control.\
"""
start = 8.53
duration = 8.425

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Its central promise is accountability: once a message is accepted, its \
journey and outcome give operators evidence they can act on.\
"""
start = 17.135
duration = 9.95

[[scene]]
file = "scene-03.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
For a CEO, the question is what happens to the business when a system \
exchange stops.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 5.775

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Xmip focuses on accountable outcomes, recovery and organizational choice."
start = 5.955
duration = 5.425

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
A practical evaluation connects those principles to a real process, its \
owner and its business impact.\
"""
start = 11.56
duration = 6.975

[[scene]]
file = "scene-04.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "For a CIO, Xmip keeps infrastructure decisions within the organization."
start = 0
duration = 5.7

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Nodes can be placed close to systems, at remote sites or on chosen hosting \
infrastructure.\
"""
start = 5.88
duration = 7.225

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Open implementation and recorded architecture make it possible to assess \
the platform and understand how it evolves.\
"""
start = 13.285
duration = 8.9

[[scene]]
file = "scene-05.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Consider an illustrative order travelling from a sales system to a \
warehouse.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 4.875

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A Receive Location accepts the stream, and Xmip persists a message."
start = 5.055
duration = 4.675

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Matching subscriptions open journeys to the destinations that want it."
start = 9.91
duration = 4.75

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A Send Location attempts delivery to the warehouse."
start = 14.84
duration = 3.85

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
That journey gives an interrupted exchange a place and an outcome to \
investigate.\
"""
start = 18.87
duration = 5.3

[[scene]]
file = "scene-06.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Acceptance is the handover of responsibility."
start = 0
duration = 3.975

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Before it, the sender owns the stream."
start = 4.155
duration = 3.05

[[scene.caption]]
text = "After it, Xmip persists a message and records its progress."
start = 7.385
duration = 4.625

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Keeping refusal distinct from a later delivery failure helps both \
organizations understand which side should act next.\
"""
start = 12.19
duration = 8.525

[[scene]]
file = "scene-07.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A subscription expresses which messages a destination wants."
start = 0
duration = 4.3

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Each match opens a journey, while an unmatched message remains available \
for replay.\
"""
start = 4.48
duration = 5.65

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Operators can pause a subscription without discarding its work, then \
resume the held messages in the order they arrived.\
"""
start = 10.31
duration = 7.825

[[scene]]
file = "scene-08.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Recovery starts with the outcome."
start = 0
duration = 2.775

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A routing issue calls for correction and replay."
start = 2.955
duration = 3.7

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
A failed delivery calls for investigation and retry, or an intentional \
dismissal.\
"""
start = 6.835
duration = 6.95

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip keeps those actions distinct, while configured attempts and backoff \
handle repeated delivery attempts.\
"""
start = 13.965
duration = 7.625

[[scene]]
file = "scene-09.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "An Xmip Application describes the integration itself."
start = 0
duration = 3.95

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A binding places that application on a node and supplies its environment."
start = 4.13
duration = 5.15

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
This separation lets developers reason about the business exchange while \
deployment choices determine which systems, addresses and machines \
participate.\
"""
start = 9.46
duration = 10

[[scene]]
file = "scene-10.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Configuration in Visual Studio Code is a flex moment."
start = 0
duration = 4.875

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Text editing and graphical designers work with the same configuration."
start = 5.055
duration = 5.5

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Completion, validation and reference-aware renaming help developers make \
consistent changes, while Xmip’s language server supplies the rules behind \
the design.\
"""
start = 10.735
duration = 11.85

[[scene]]
file = "scene-11.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "TOML is another flex moment."
start = 0
duration = 3

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip configuration stays in readable text that teams can version, compare \
and review.\
"""
start = 3.18
duration = 6.575

[[scene.caption]]
text = "The designer works with that same source."
start = 9.935
duration = 3.075

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
This makes configuration an engineering artifact the team can understand \
and maintain together.\
"""
start = 13.19
duration = 7.275

[[scene]]
file = "scene-12.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Some exchanges need business steps as well as delivery."
start = 0
duration = 4.05

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip models these as Work Processes, designed in BPMN and compiled into \
executable units.\
"""
start = 4.23
duration = 7.225

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Their state belongs to the ledger, so waiting work does not hold a thread."
start = 11.635
duration = 4.65

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Compilation and execution exist as components; connecting them into the \
assembled service remains a project milestone.\
"""
start = 16.465
duration = 8.4

[[scene]]
file = "scene-13.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip separates how data travels, how it is represented, and what the \
integration does with it.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 7.075

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Contracts define acceptance rules, while processing expresses business \
flow.\
"""
start = 7.255
duration = 6

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Providers extend individual capabilities through explicit interfaces and a \
versioned C boundary.\
"""
start = 13.435
duration = 7.625

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
That modular architecture lets the platform evolve without treating every \
change as a replacement.\
"""
start = 21.24
duration = 7.6

[[scene]]
file = "scene-14.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip’s technology estate spans file transfer, web communication, message \
brokers, databases and industrial systems.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 8.5

[[scene.caption]]
text = "SFTP, HTTP, AMQP, Kafka, PostgreSQL and OPC UA are examples of that scope."
start = 8.68
duration = 8.1

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A site build chooses the technologies it needs."
start = 16.96
duration = 3.325

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
This is the estate’s breadth, with availability depending on the \
capability and its integration into the service.\
"""
start = 20.465
duration = 7.05

[[scene]]
file = "scene-15.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Trust is explicit at Xmip’s boundaries."
start = 0
duration = 3.325

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Parties carry identities, receive locations define what they accept, and \
outbound exchanges use their own identity.\
"""
start = 3.505
duration = 9.375

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Certificate authentication, protected storage connections and encrypted \
embedded data give that architecture concrete foundations.\
"""
start = 13.06
duration = 10

[[scene]]
file = "scene-16.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Xmip Storage gives work a persistent home."
start = 0
duration = 3.075

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
A small deployment can host storage within its own node, while other nodes \
reach it over mutual TLS.\
"""
start = 3.255
duration = 6.975

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
The ledger holds messages, journeys and pending work, separate from \
administration and audit concerns.\
"""
start = 10.41
duration = 6.7

[[scene]]
file = "scene-17.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "A deployment is a composition of roles and capabilities."
start = 0
duration = 4.65

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Executing brings the message stages together in one process, while other \
roles serve storage, observation and operation.\
"""
start = 4.83
duration = 9.075

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Site builds select the target and technologies; configuration determines \
what the node starts.\
"""
start = 14.085
duration = 7.075

[[scene]]
file = "scene-18.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Cross-operating-system working is a shared flex moment."
start = 0
duration = 3.925

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Xmip’s architecture targets Windows, Linux and Mac computers with one \
integration model.\
"""
start = 4.105
duration = 6.075

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Site builds select the roles and technologies for a developer machine, an \
edge gateway or a server.\
"""
start = 10.36
duration = 6.525

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Packaging and validation progress separately on each platform."
start = 17.065
duration = 4.525

[[scene]]
file = "scene-19.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Offline operation is part of Xmip’s design."
start = 0
duration = 3.4

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Packages can be prepared where dependencies are reachable, then brought \
into disconnected environments.\
"""
start = 3.58
duration = 6.575

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Internet access is an explicit capability, supporting sites where \
connectivity is restricted, intermittent or deliberately absent.\
"""
start = 10.335
duration = 8.8

[[scene]]
file = "scene-20.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Operators can choose a command line, PowerShell, desktop or web interface \
without learning a different platform model.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 8.825

[[scene.caption]]
text = "The same scopes and meanings guide investigation."
start = 9.005
duration = 3.975

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Automation and visual inspection become different ways to work with the \
same operational evidence.\
"""
start = 13.16
duration = 7.35

[[scene]]
file = "scene-21.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Operations in your phone is a flex moment in Xmip’s design."
start = 0
duration = 4.3

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
The mobile host brings the same cluster health and scope navigation to \
Android and iPhone targets.\
"""
start = 4.48
duration = 6.95

[[scene.caption]]
text = "It follows nodes remotely in the Observer role."
start = 11.61
duration = 3.45

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Device validation remains a project milestone, while the principle stays \
the same: understand the affected scope wherever you are.\
"""
start = 15.24
duration = 8.475

[[scene]]
file = "scene-22.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Health should tell an operator where to look and what to do."
start = 0
duration = 4.15

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Xmip uses named conditions and scope navigation."
start = 4.33
duration = 4.425

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
A parent holding points into its children, where the affected resource and \
its reason help distinguish a deliberate pause from strain or failure.\
"""
start = 8.935
duration = 9.9

[[scene]]
file = "scene-23.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Current observation and audit answer different questions."
start = 0
duration = 3.95

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Observation shows what is happening now."
start = 4.13
duration = 3

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Audit records actions and outcomes over time."
start = 7.31
duration = 3.45

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Chained program records, verification and journey evidence help the team \
investigate a specific exchange instead of guessing from disconnected \
symptoms.\
"""
start = 10.94
duration = 10.275

[[scene]]
file = "scene-24.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = "Xmip also exposes read-only access through the Model Context Protocol."
start = 0
duration = 6.275

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Clients can inspect health, measurements, audit and journeys through tools \
and scoped resources.\
"""
start = 6.455
duration = 6.85

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
The behavior follows the command line, and each answer is audited, keeping \
observation connected to established operational controls.\
"""
start = 13.485
duration = 9.875

[[scene]]
file = "scene-25.wav"

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
Open source is a flex moment because teams can inspect, improve and extend \
Xmip.\
"""
start = 0
duration = 5.95

[[scene.caption]]
text = """\
The platform is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, \
